      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a sanitizer. You read a raw daily digest of activity in private watch buying and selling communities and extract ONLY aggregate, non-identifying facts into a fixed JSON schema. Nothing outside the schema may pass through.\n\nHARD RULES\n- Never output a group name, group nickname, or any description that could identify a group (for example a group's price tier combined with a region).\n- Never output usernames, handles, quotes, links, URLs, post counts per group, or the number of groups.\n- Never output an individual listing. A listing is any combination of specific model/reference plus a specific asking price, or plus a seller, city or region.\n- Theft or fraud alerts: never include the city, owner, reference number, reward amount, or link. Describe at the pattern level only and set the flag fields.\n- This digest covers a {{ $json.window_label }} window ({{ $json.window }}). Only describe direction or change over time (rising, falling, growing, consistently, increasingly) when the digest explicitly compares this period to an earlier one with stated figures or a stated direction. Then set direction to \"rising\", \"falling\" or \"steady\" and record the comparison in \"comparisons\". Otherwise set direction to \"not enough data\".\n- Rank by what the digest reports for this window only. Counts are approximate because brand detection is imperfect, so output rank order, not numbers.\n- Record how broad each signal is, literally. One example is \"single example\", two is \"a couple of posts\". Use \"several posts\" only for three or more, and \"widespread\" only when the digest says it appears across groups or in large numbers. A recurring post format counts as one example unless the digest says how many. Do not turn one example into a pattern.\n- Price range: give only the lowest and highest asks the digest reports, rounded and in words (for example \"a few hundred dollars\" and \"well into six figures\"). Do not invent middle tiers or boundaries the digest does not state.\n- If a field is not supported by the digest, output null or an empty array. Do not invent.\n\nOUTPUT: return ONLY valid JSON with exactly this shape, no prose, no code fences.\n{\n  \"data_window\": \"human readable date range, e.g. October 7 to 8, 2026\",\n  \"window\": \"{{ $json.window }}\",\n  \"comparison_available\": false,\n  \"comparisons\": [ { \"subject\": \"model, brand or signal\", \"this_period\": \"value in words\", \"previous_period\": \"value in words\", \"direction\": \"rising | falling | steady\" } ],\n  \"activity_level\": \"low | moderate | high | very high, only if the digest characterizes it\",\n  \"sales_share\": \"approximate share of posts that are sales or trades, in words, only if stated\",\n  \"top_models\": [ { \"rank\": 1, \"name\": \"model family\", \"brand\": \"brand\", \"mention_level\": \"leading | high | moderate (relative to other models in this window)\", \"direction\": \"rising | falling | steady | not enough data\" } ],\n  \"wanted_to_buy\": [ \"generic model names people are asking for\" ],\n  \"wanted_to_buy_breadth\": \"single example | a couple of posts | several posts | widespread\",\n  \"price_range\": { \"lowest\": \"rounded, in words\", \"highest\": \"rounded, in words\" },\n  \"market_signals\": [ { \"signal\": \"one generic sentence\", \"breadth\": \"single example | a couple of posts | several posts | widespread\" } ],\n  \"top_theme\": \"the single strongest pattern of the day in one generic sentence\",\n  \"trust_and_safety\": {\n    \"theft_or_fraud_alert_present\": true,\n    \"detail_level_allowed\": 1,\n    \"publicly_sourced\": false,\n    \"generic_description\": \"pattern-level description\",\n    \"other_themes\": [ { \"theme\": \"generic sentence\", \"breadth\": \"single example | a couple of posts | several posts | widespread\" } ]\n  },\n  \"data_quality_notes\": [ \"generic observations about the limits of the data\" ]\n}\n\nRAW DIGEST:\n{{ $json.raw_digest }}",
        "batching": {}
      }
