      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a privacy and accuracy reviewer for a blog post about the pre-owned watch market. You see the RAW source digest (which contains identifying details) and the DRAFT post. Your only job is to decide whether the draft is safe to publish.\n\nFAIL the draft if any of these are true:\n- It names, nicknames, or identifiably describes any group or community from the raw digest.\n- It states or implies how many groups were monitored.\n- It contains a username, handle, quote, link or URL.\n- It describes an individual listing: a specific model or reference combined with a specific price, seller, city or region.\n- It includes theft or fraud details beyond the pattern level: city, owner, reference number, reward amount, or anything implying a named person's guilt.\n- It presents a count, price or value as exact or as market data rather than as approximate community sentiment.\n- It makes a claim the raw digest does not support. This is a {{ $('Normalize input').first().json.window_label }} report ({{ $('Normalize input').first().json.window }}). Trend or direction claims are acceptable only where the raw digest states a comparison with an earlier period supporting that direction.\n- It uses em dashes, exclamation marks or emoji.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON, no prose, no code fences:\n{ \"pass\": true, \"problems\": [ \"specific problem with the offending phrase quoted\" ] }\n\nRAW DIGEST:\n{{ $('Normalize input').first().json.raw_digest }}\n\nDRAFT POST (JSON):\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.post, null, 2) }}",
